/* Known -W<name> spellings (positive form, without any "no-" prefix).
 * Curated from gcc 8's C warning surface — the names configure scripts
 * and Makefiles actually pass. Sprint 26 uses this ONLY for the
 * unknown-flag policy (-W<unknown> warns and continues); Sprint 37 wires
 * real semantics onto the same rows. -Wno-<anything> is silently
 * accepted regardless (gcc parity — flag probes depend on it).
 * W(name) — keep sorted. */
